NISAR (NASA-ISRO Synthetic Aperture Radar)
  Data provided by NASA/JPL-Caltech and the Indian Space Research Organisation
  (ISRO), archived and distributed by the Alaska Satellite Facility (ASF) DAAC
  and NASA Earthdata. NASA Earth science data are free and open, with no
  restrictions on use: https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/about/esdis-policy

  Required acknowledgement (adapt when finalising the submission):
  "NISAR data courtesy of NASA/JPL-Caltech and ISRO, accessed through the ASF
  DAAC and NASA Earthdata."

Other Space Agency Partner data (e.g. CSA RADARSAT-1/RCM, CONAE SAOCOM) is used
only where explicitly permitted by the provider's data policy; each source and
its license is recorded in docs/data-sources.md.

